# Rust build output. Large, per-machine, and regenerated by `cargo build`.
src-tauri/target/
# Written by tauri-build on every compile.
src-tauri/gen/

# What `npm run stage:sidecar` produces. Both are copies of things the repo
# already has - a ~92 MB Node runtime and the compiled `dist/src` - and neither
# is a source. Committing either would put a binary in git history that is
# rebuilt on every machine anyway.
src-tauri/binaries/
src-tauri/host/

# The 1024px square `make-icon.mjs` draws. The script is the source; this is its
# output, and it is regenerated in one command.
#
# `src-tauri/icons/` IS tracked, even though it is derived from this file. The
# derivation needs the Tauri CLI and a step nobody would think to run, and a
# fresh clone that cannot build for want of an icon is a worse trade than eleven
# small PNGs in git. Same reasoning as the bundled woff2 files.
src-tauri/icon-source.png
